# ⚠ DO NOT ADD `merge=union` HERE AND THEN RELY ON IT.
#
# GITHUB'S PR MERGE IGNORES .gitattributes MERGE DRIVERS. Your local `git merge` honours them, so
# a union-merged shared file tests clean on one machine and then conflicts on the workflow this
# harness prescribes (branch + PR). In the project this harness was extracted from that cost two
# full PR re-rolls in a single day (2026-07-14) before anyone worked out why — the pattern looks
# like it works right up until two agents actually use it.
#
# THE FIX IS STRUCTURAL, NOT A MERGE DRIVER: give each concurrent writer its OWN FILE, so there is
# nothing to merge.
#
#   features/<id>.json          one live ticket per file
#   features/archive/<id>.json  one archived ticket per file   (was: feature_list.archive.jsonl)
#   progress/<stamp>-<name>.md  one session entry per file      (was: PROGRESS.md, appended)
#
# DECISIONS.md is still a single append-only file and is therefore still exposed to this. It is
# left that way deliberately — entries are rare, and the log reads badly split across files — but
# EXPECT A CONFLICT THERE when two branches both append, and resolve it by keeping both entries.
# If your project appends to it often, split it the same way as the three above.
#
# Nothing in this file sets a merge driver, and that absence is the decision.
